# nr-exthost-imaging-still: what the lead applies after the wave.
#
# The crate mixdog-imaging now links libwebp (the lossy WebP encoder libvips writes with), so the build needs the crate
# libwebp-sys. It is in the offline cargo cache (libwebp-sys-0.9.6.crate, MIT; the bundled libwebp is BSD-3-Clause);
# its only build dependencies, cc and glob 0.3, are already in Cargo.lock (cc 1.x with the `parallel` feature the
# workspace hack already unifies; glob 0.3.4). No other crate is added.
#
# 1. native/core/Cargo.toml, [workspace.dependencies], after the line that begins `image = {`, add:
libwebp-sys = "=0.9.6" # nr-exthost-imaging-still: lossy WebP encode for image.still renditions and resized WebP inputs (bundled libwebp, C built with cc); default features (std, parallel, neon)
#
# 2. native/core/Cargo.lock: let cargo add the entry offline (`cargo metadata --offline` or any `cargo build --offline`
#    without --locked once; then the build is --locked again): a [[package]] name = "libwebp-sys" version = "0.9.6"
#    with dependencies "cc" and "glob", and "libwebp-sys" in the dependency list of mixdog-imaging.
#
# 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml: regenerate with the repository's hakari command if it lists
#    cc or glob features per target; libwebp-sys itself needs no feature the hack does not already unify.
#
# The crate's own manifest (crates/mixdog-imaging/Cargo.toml) already says `libwebp-sys = { workspace = true }`;
# until step 1 is applied that crate does not resolve.
#
# Nothing else: no workspace member (mixdog-imaging is one), no index.ts registration, no protocol row, no entry in
# SERVICE_PENDING (the image.still method is served by a later wave's wiring, which calls
# mixdog_imaging::still::rendition_spec and still::encode_still).
#
# The fixture set native/core/fixtures/image-still is new: if native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json indexes the sets,
# refresh it (the recorder writes image-still/MANIFEST.json itself).
